{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HSb6bxgvP7DkPMzGj9FnoC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. This project derives specs from C source code, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract, specify, synthesize, verify). `cmd/` holds per-utility Go packages, `pkg/testutils/` provides the differential testing harness, `pkg/sys/` wraps platform-specific syscalls, `pkg/format/` handles output formatting. Specs live in `docs/`, build targets in `magefiles/`.\n\n**Implementation state (from source code):**\n- **Done:** pkg/testutils, pkg/sys (file metadata), pkg/format (columns, colors, sizes), cmd/cat, cmd/wc, cmd/sponge, cmd/du, cmd/version\n- **Spec complete, code pending:** cmd/ls (rel04.0 core, rel04.1 extended)\n- **Specs pending (no PRD):** rel02.0 (true/false/yes/basename/dirname), rel02.1 (tee), rel02.2 (head/seq)\n\n**Current release:** The earliest incomplete release with actionable specs is **rel04.0** (ls core). Releases 02.0-02.2 have pending specs, and PRD authoring is human-guided (DD5), so no code tasks can be proposed for them.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\n- rel00.0, 01.1, 01.2, 01.3, 03.0: All code exists in source_code -- done.\n- rel02.0, 02.1, 02.2: Specs pending. PRDs are human-authored (DD5), so these are blocked on the human operator.\n- **rel04.0 (ls core): spec_complete, code not started** -- this is the next actionable release.\n- Per P2, implementation and tests must be split. The first task is `cmd/ls/main.go` (implementation).\n- ls is complex; this first task covers only basic directory listing, sorting, argument handling, and hidden-file filtering (~150-200 lines).\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"prd008-ls R1.1-R1.4: Directory entry listing, argument handling, sorting, and one-per-line output for cmd/ls\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-04.0.yaml (ls core test suite -- contains PRD cross-references and exact requirement IDs)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel04.0-uc001-ls.yaml (ls core use case -- contains PRD reference)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (find the ls PRD; filename follows prdNNN-ls.yaml convention; the test suite and use case above reference it by name)\n      - cmd/du/main.go (implementation pattern: directory traversal with os.ReadDir, SIGPIPE handler, argument loop, reportError to stderr)\n      - cmd/cat/main.go (implementation pattern: options struct, flag parsing, buffered stdout with flush error detection, exit code accumulation)\n      - pkg/sys/fileinfo.go (Stat/Lstat API for file-vs-directory detection on arguments)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/ls/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Basic ls: directory reading, alphabetical sorting, hidden-file filtering (-a, -A), one-per-line output\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Read directory entries using os.ReadDir and print entry names to stdout, one per line. Sort entries alphabetically using byte-order comparison (matching GNU ls behavior under LC_ALL=C).\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Default to \\\".\\\" when no command-line arguments are given. Process multiple arguments in command-line order. When listing more than one directory, print a header line in the format \\\"<dir>:\\\" before each directory's entries, with a blank line between directory groups.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Exclude entries starting with \\\".\\\" by default. Support -a flag (show all entries including . and ..) and -A flag (show all entries except . and ..). When a command-line argument is a non-directory file, print its name as a single line without a header.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Exit 0 on success. Exit 1 if any argument produces an error (nonexistent path, permission denied). Write per-path error messages to stderr in the format \\\"ls: <path>: <error>\\\". Handle SIGPIPE by exiting with code 0.\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"Buffer stdout output using bufio.NewWriter. Flush at exit and set exit code to 1 if flush produces a write error, matching the output error detection pattern in cmd/cat and cmd/wc.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Follow the main.go structure from cmd/cat and cmd/du: package comment referencing the ls PRD, import block, options struct, SIGPIPE goroutine, flag.Parse, argument processing loop with accumulated exit code, os.Exit.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use os.ReadDir for directory listing. Re-sort entry names with sort.Strings to guarantee byte-order sorting under LC_ALL=C, even though os.ReadDir already returns entries sorted by name.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Output one entry per line in this initial task. Multi-column layout (pkg/format.Columns), long format (-l), color output (pkg/format.FileTypeColor), and additional flags are deferred to subsequent tasks.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/ls/main.go compiles with go build ./cmd/ls/ and produces a working binary.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Running the binary with no arguments lists current directory entries alphabetically, one per line, excluding entries starting with \\\".\\\".\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"-a shows all entries including . and .. in sorted position. -A shows entries starting with \\\".\\\" but excludes the literal . and .. entries.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"A nonexistent path argument produces exit code 1 and a diagnostic on stderr matching the format \\\"ls: <path>: <error-message>\\\".\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Two or more directory arguments produce a header line (\\\"<dir>:\\\") before each directory's entries, with a blank line separating groups.\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"A file argument (not a directory) prints its name as a single output line without a header.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":72668,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":72668},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b8d3747d-f978-490e-96e3-7d0be17639ee","uuid":"d2fbbba6-d974-43cc-86a5-c9babc2671bf"}
